CS1,0 $ $ MICROSCOPIC KEY TO THE STAINING SPECIES OF LYOPHYLLUM
1,0$ Croquis micros de Heinz Clémençon, cf Mycotaxon 18, 379-437 $$f"LYOPHYLLUM_PN-STAINING_ SPECIES.jpg"
1,0 $ a Spores punctate-rough, finely warted, or spiny $ L. scabrisporum
1,2 $ b Spores smooth
2,0 $ a Adaxial spore face rhomboidal, supra-apicular plane or depression usually well-developed $ L. geminum
2,3 $ b Adaxial spore face round to elliptic, with round or pointed base but not rhomboidal
3,4 $ a Superficial hyphae of stipe frequently agglutinated into massive, erect fascicles; pileipellis 30-60 um thick, gelatinous, with erect, isolated, clustered or intertwisted hairs
3,6 $ b Superficial hyphae of stipe different; when arranged in erect groups or tufts, then not intertwisted and pileipellis not gelatinous
4,0 $ a Pileus densely covered with erect, complex knots of braided hyphae $ L. furfurellum
4,5 $ b Pileus without such knots
5,0 $ a Pileipellis with a few scattered, cylindrical, short and inconspicuous hairs $ L. stenosporum
5,0 $ b Pileipellis with separated, dense clusters of small, repent to erect, contorted, clavate, irregular hairs with colorless or brown walls $ L. investitum
6,7 $ a (3b) Pileus hygrophanous, margin striatulate when wet; spores asymmetrically ovate in side view, thickest towards the apicular end, thinner at the apex, dimensions in the range 6.2-8.7 x 4.3-5.9 um, Q = 1.3-1.8; pileipellis an ixocutis, 30-45 um thick; basidia 25-35 um long
6,8 $ b Pileus not hygrophanous or margin not striatulate when wet or spores of different shape or pileipellis not gelatinous or thicker than 45 um, or basidia longer than 35 um
7,0 $ a Odor distinctly of potatoes, pileus dark fuliginous except at margin, fading to grayish brown, surface uneven and pitted $ L. conoideospermum
7,0 $ b Odor not distinct, pileus very pale watery gray with pallid margin, pallid overall when faded, surface smooth $ L. pallidum
8,0 $ a (6b) Odor strongly disagreeable rancid-farinaceous; stipe canescent over a pale blue-gray surface by long, cylindrical-wavy hairs, and hollow; basidia 36-40 x 7-8 um; ixocutis 60-80 um thick $ L. canescentipes
8,9 $ b Odor not strongly disagreeable rancid farinaceous or stipe not canescent or stipe not hollow or basidia of different dimensions, or ixocutis 60-80 um thick not present
9,0 $ a Odor spermatic, Inocybe-like; pileus 1-2.5 cm broad, very cartilaginous; spores short-ellipsoidal without supra-apicular depression, 5.7-8.0 x 4.7-5.5 um, Q = 1.2-1.6; pileipellis gelatinous $ L. chondrocephalum
9,10 $ b Odor not spermatic; pileus larger
10,0 $ a Odor of green corn; spores spherical to short-ellipsoidal: all of the following criteria apply simultaneously to at least 90% of the spores of a preparation: Q=1-1.45, difference between spore-length and width at most 2 um, supra-apicular depression absent $ L. leptosarx
10,11 $ b Odors various or not distinct; spores elongate-ellipsoidal, frequently asymmetrical: at least one of the following criteria applies to at least half of the spores of a preparation: either Q greater than 1.45, or difference between spore length and width over 2 um, or spores with a supra-apicular depression
11,12 $ a Stipe naked, even under the gills; odor farinaceous-rancid; cap 2.5-4 cm broad, hygrophanous, dark fuliginous, thin; gills adnate, subdistant; spores 6.5-8.7 x 3.5-5.3 um, with rounded base, without supra-apicular depression; basidia 27-33 um long; marginal cells hyphoid, 3-6 um broad, scattered to rare
11,13 $ b Not all the characters simultaneously present; stipe covered with some hairs or even a tomentum, at least below the gills
12,0 $ a Pileipellis not gelatinous, hyphae 2-4 um thick, smooth, colorless, radially arranged, covered with a few interwoven hyphae 5-8 um wide and with brown incrusting pigments and with numerous colorless, smooth, contorted or ramified, erect, 2-3 um broad hairs $ L. fistulosum
12,0 $ b Pileipellis gelatinous, superficial hyphae 2 to 3 um broad and smooth; hairs rare, scattered, inconspicuous $ L. gracile
13,0 $ a (11b) Cap margin translucent-striate; stipe hollow, pruinose at apex; spores with a pointed apicular base, 6.7-9.3 x 3.3-5.0 um, Q = 1.6-2.2 $ L. semitale
13,14 $ b Other combination of characters, spore base round
14,0 $ a Pileipellis not gelatinous $ L. chamaeleon
14,15 $ b Pileipellis gelatinous
15,0 $ a Odor and taste not distinct $ L. piceum
15,16 $ b Odor farinaceous
16,0 $ a Basidia 37-42 um long; hyphae of pileipellis interwoven $ L. lubricum
16,17 $ b Basidia 29-36 um long
17,0 $ a Cap with erect, cylindrical to slightly irregular hairs, 30-40 x 3-4 um $ L. acutipes
17,0 $ b Cap without erect hairs $ L. solidipes



CS2,0$ MACROSCOPIC KEY TO THE STAINING SPECIES OF LYOPHYLLUM
1,0 $ a Tricholomatoid stature, dry cap with center pallid to dingy gray and margin pallid, cap becoming blackish where bruised, pale ashy gray flesh that becomes darker where bruised, close, pale olive gray gills that stain bluish and finally black, pallid fibrillose stipe that is darker where handled or when old, faint disagreeable odor, somewhat cespitose growth, (spores punctate-rough, finely warted or spiny) $ L. scabrisporum
1,2 $ b Not as above
2,0 $ a Fresh cap dark sooty, lubricous, and bald, gills broad gray becoming blackish where bruised or when old, stipe whitish gray darkening where bruised and appressed-fibrillose at first, odor faintly farinaceous, growth cespitose $ L. furfurellum
2,3 $ b Adaxial spore face round to elliptic, with round or pointed base but not rhomboidal
3,0 $ a Odor of potatoes $ L. conoideospermum
3,4 $ b Odor farinaceous, spermatic, green corn, or mild
4,5 $ a Spermatic or green corn odor
4,6 $ b Farinaceous or mild odor
5,0 $ a Green corn odor, flesh thin, stains blue and finally black $ L. leptosarx
5,0 $ b Green corn odor, flesh slowly gray when bruised $ L. geminum var. olens
5,0 $ c Spermatic odor, cap cartilaginous, all parts stain directly black $ L. chondrocephalum
6,7 $ a (4b) Farinaceous odor
6,14 $ b Mild odor
7,0 $ a Cap hygrophanous, gray brown to dark brown, moist to buttery, margin translucent-striate, gills pallid or grayish, stem pruinose at apex, often in mountains $ L. semitale
7,8 $ b Not with this combination of characters
8,0 $ a Cap dark sooty-gray, when broken cap staining immediately bluish gray to black, pale gray gills, stem hoary over a pale blue-gray surface $ L. canescentipes
8,9 $ b Not with this combination of characters
9,10 $ a Stem solid when mature
9,11 $ b Stem hollow or stuffed with pith when mature
10,0 $ a Cap pale gray to blackish, (with erect, cylindrical to slightly irregular hairs, 30-40 x 3-4 um) $ L. acutipes
10,0 $ b Cap buffy brown to olive brown, (without erect hairs) $ L. solidipes
11,0 $ a (9b) Cap flesh not changing in color when cut, gills staining bluish gray when cut or bruised $ L. gracile
11,12 $ b Cap flesh changing in color when cut, gills staining various colors when cut or bruised
12,0 $ a Pileipellis Gills staining yellowish then bluish $ L. chamaeleon
12,13 $ b Gills staining black
13,0 $ a Cap 4-7 cm broad, stipe 6-11 cm x 1.0-1.6 cm at top, narrowing down to pointed, somewhat rooting base, stuffed becoming hollow, pallid soon darkening and dingy, innately fibrillose often lacerating into scales that become cinnamon buff $ L. lubricum
13,0 $ b Cap 2.5-4 cm broad, stipe 2-5 cm x 0.4-1.0 cm, hollow, wavy and compressed or grooved, fragile, pale dingy gray (blackening when old), bald $ L. fistulosum
14,15 $ a (6b) Gills somewhat decurrent, caps medium to dark gray (fuliginous or sooty) when moist
14,16 $ b Gills adnate, caps pale gray or drab when moist
15,0 $ a Flesh staining blackish $ L. piceum
15,0 $ b Odor farinaceous $ L. stenosporum
16,0 $ a (14b) Cap drab when moist, stem surface pallid from thin hoary coating $ L. investitum
16,17 $ b Cap pale gray when moist, hoary coating on stem not recorded
17,0 $ a Cap lubricous to viscid when wet, flesh turning bluish gray, stem surface not discoloring noticeably when bruised, (spores elliptic 6.2-7.4(8.5) x 4.5-5.2(6.5) um) $ L. pallidum
17,0 $ b Cap moist, flesh turning gray, stem surface whitish becoming gray where handled, (spores fusoid-ventricose 8.8-11.6 x 4.1-6.2 um) $ L. geminum var. geminum
